From 614181c6f35dcf29d6735d795be79e14f34ec07c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:55:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libcamera: software_isp: Report colour sums in 8-bit units

The statistics of unpacked 10 and 12 bit Bayer formats sum the raw
sample values, while the black level and the histogram the IPA works
with are in 8-bit units. The AWB subtracted a quarter of the real black
level from 10-bit sums: on the S5K4H5YC, black at 64 out of 1023, a dim
indoor scene that needs a blue gain of 2.29 got 1.50, and the picture
kept a colour cast that grew as the light fell.

Shift the sums down to 8 bits per sample at the end of the frame, as
the packed formats already sample them, the same way current upstream
libcamera does.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
Base-commit: 3becb16c1fa22d79a4d7eeb75a36fc895b4b7abf
Source: https://github.com/alessandro-fontana/android_external_libcamera/commit/614181c6f35dcf29d6735d795be79e14f34ec07c

